WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.167
In this walkthrough we'll net
settlements down to a single payment,
and read the result, in the OpenTRMS Workbench.

2
00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:17.533
Netting reduces many payments to one. Rather
than settling twenty amounts with the same
counterparty on the same day, you settle the difference.

3
00:00:17.533 --> 00:00:28.167
Only eligible settlements are listed. Each row shows the
amount and whether it is money going out or coming in,
which is what makes netting possible in the first place.

4
00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:40.200
Netting is bilateral, so the counterparty filter comes
first. You net against one institution at a time —
amounts owed to different counterparties cannot offset each other.

5
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:50.833
Select Visible takes everything the filters have left
on screen, which is quicker than ticking rows one by
one, and the count keeps track of what you have chosen.

6
00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:56.733
Executing the netting would create
a netting set from that selection.

7
00:00:56.733 --> 00:01:09.067
Netting Sets is where the results live. Each set records the
gross payable, the gross receivable, and the net amount that
will actually move, along with how many settlements it replaced.

8
00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:16.867
That completes Netting Settlements. Every surface
shown here can also be opened from the agent
panel on the right, by asking for it in plain English.
